  vars-on-top  All 'var' declarations must be at the top of the function scope. A `var` is hoisted to the top of its function whatever line it is written on, so a declaration buried in a loop or a branch reads as scoped to that block and is not. Writing them together at the top makes the text say what the engine already does.

